## Teach terms inline (glossary on first use)

Whenever a domain word appears, teach it once per file (or per method if the file is huge):

```csharp
// Ghost — NetCode's name for a networked entity replica on client or server (not a visual "ghost sprite").
// RPC (Remote Procedure Call) — client asks server to run an action; server validates then applies.
// ScriptableObject — Unity asset file holding design data (stats, catalogs), loaded at runtime.
// MonoBehaviour — Unity component on a GameObject; runs on main thread with Update/LateUpdate.
// World (ECS) — DOTS container for entities/components/systems; separate from Unity "scene".
// Fixed step — simulation tick at fixed dt (e.g. 60 Hz); movement should use this, not frame delta.
// Presentation — phase after sim where transforms are smoothed for rendering.
```

If two concepts interact, say both:
```csharp
// ShipInputApplySystem runs in GhostInputSystemGroup — NetCode's slot for copying player input onto ghosts before prediction.
```

---

## What to comment (checklist for every code construct)

Apply to **all** topics — not only ship movement:

| Construct | Teach in comments |
|-----------|-------------------|
| **Class / file** | Responsibility, which assembly/build (client, server, editor), entry points |
| **Fields & SerializeField** | Source of truth, default meaning, inspector vs code-set |
| **Properties** | Computed vs stored; thread/world safety |
| **Constructors / Awake / OnEnable** | Order vs other components; what must exist first |
| **Start / OnDisable / OnDestroy** | Cleanup, unsubscribe, release native refs |
| **Update / LateUpdate / FixedUpdate** | Why this loop rate; what must NOT move here (sim authority) |
| **Coroutines / async** | What waits; what thread; cancellation |
| **if / else / switch** | Gameplay or network meaning of each branch |
| **Loops** | What one iteration represents; early-exit reason |
| **LINQ / allocations** | If hot path, note cost; if cold, say "runs once at load" |
| **Try/catch** | What failure looks like for player or server |
| **Math / vectors** | Units, space (world vs local), normalized or not |
| **Queries** | Included/excluded entities; performance note if broad |
| **Component reads/writes** | Who owns writes; prediction vs authority |
| **Instantiate / Destroy** | Pool vs spawn; network spawn if relevant |
| **UI bindings** | What player sees; what ECS/RPC it triggers |
| **ScriptableObject fields** | Designer-tunable vs code constant |
| **#if UNITY_EDITOR / SERVER** | Which build strips this; why the split exists |

