## Topic guides (all areas — same depth)

### ECS / Systems (`Assets/Scripts/ECS/**`)

- File summary: world filter (`ClientSimulation`, `ServerSimulation`, `Presentation`), system group, `[UpdateBefore/After]`.
- `OnCreate`: what singletons/queries are cached and why caching matters for performance.
- `OnUpdate`: per-phase comments — query → read components → write components → dispose.
- Every `WithAll` / `WithNone`: who is in the query and why.
- Burst: `[BurstCompile]` meaning; what cannot run in Burst (managed strings, EntityManager in hot path).
- Pair client prediction with server authority by name.

### ECS / Components & Authoring

- Each `IComponentData` field: gameplay meaning, units, who writes, ghost-serialized or local-only.
- Bakers: what GameObject/prefab data becomes which entity components at bake time.
- Ghost fields: what replicates to clients; prediction importance if applicable.

### NetCode & session (`NetCode/**`, RPCs, session managers)

- Connection lifecycle: listen, join, disconnect, host vs dedicated server.
- RPC handlers: what client sends, what server validates, what can cheat if missing.
- Bootstrap / dedicated server: `#if UNITY_SERVER` paths; what runs headless only.

### Game / presentation bridges (`Game/**`, visual appliers, `EcsWorldVisualizer`)

- `[HYBRID]` — ECS sim state → GameObject proxy; **render only**, never drive sim.
- Which transform source (presentation cache vs sim) and why.
- Per-frame sync: what is cosmetic smoothing vs forbidden movement smoothing.

### UI (`UI/**`)

- What screen/panel this is; which player state it reflects.
- Button/handler → which RPC or local action; server authority for gameplay changes.
- Mobile vs desktop branches if present.

### Input (`Input/**`)

- How input becomes `ShipInput` or UI events; client-only path.
- Dead zones, sticks, hold-to-shoot — tie to feel and NetCode input buffer.

### Data (`Data/**`, ScriptableObjects, catalogs)

- What designers edit in Inspector; what systems consume at runtime.
- Cache/load path; when data is baked vs read live.

### Services (`Services/**`, ads, friends, platform)

- External SDK boundaries; what is stubbed in editor.
- Threading and main-thread dispatch back to Unity.

### Camera (`Camera/**`)

- Follow target source (presentation pose); not sim for local owner if rule forbids.

### Editor (`Editor/**`, `ECS/Editor/**`)

- `[EDITOR]` — menu item purpose; what asset/scene it modifies; safe to run when.

### Diagnostics (`Diagnostics/**`)

- What gets logged; server file log vs client console; performance impact.

