## Examples across file kinds

### ECS system (good density)

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Server-authoritative ship movement. Runs the shared motor for every ship ghost each fixed step,
/// before Unity Physics integrates hull position. Paired with ShipClientPredictedMovementSystem (client).
/// World: ServerSimulation. Group: PredictedFixedStepSimulationSystemGroup, before PhysicsSystemGroup.
/// </summary>
[UpdateBefore(typeof(PhysicsSystemGroup))]
public partial struct ShipMovementSystem : ISystem
{
    public void OnUpdate(ref SystemState state)
    {
        // --- Fixed timestep ---
        // [UNITY] TimeStep from FixedStepSimulationSystemGroup — same dt as client prediction.
        float dt = SystemAPI.Time.DeltaTime;

        // --- Motor pass (velocity + rotation only) ---
        // [ECS/DOTS] RefRW = read/write access; we mutate PhysicsVelocity and LocalTransform.Rotation.
        // [TITAN-ORBIT] Position is NOT integrated here — PhysicsSystemGroup owns Position.
        foreach (var (transform, velocity, input, entity) in SystemAPI.Query<...>().WithAll<ShipTag, Simulate>())
        {
            // [NETCODE] Simulate — entity participates in prediction on client; server still uses tag for same query shape.
            ShipMovementLogic.StepShip(ref transform.ValueRW, ref velocity.ValueRW, input, dt, ...);
        }
    }
}
```

### MonoBehaviour bridge (good density)

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Copies the local ship's presentation transform from ECS into the camera follow target.
/// Runs in LateUpdate after ShipVisualSyncSystem has written the presentation cache.
/// Client only — server has no camera.
/// </summary>
public class CameraFollowEcs : MonoBehaviour
{
    [SerializeField] Transform followTarget;

    void LateUpdate()
    {
        // --- Resolve local ship pose ---
        // [HYBRID] Read presentation cache, not sim LocalTransform — avoids jitter on predicted owner.
        if (!GhostPresentationTransformCache.TryGetLocalShip(out var pose))
            return; // [STANDARD] No ship yet (loading, dead, or not spawned).

        // --- Apply to camera rig ---
        // [UNITY] followTarget is the camera pivot in the scene hierarchy.
        followTarget.SetPositionAndRotation(pose.Position, pose.Rotation);
    }
}
```

### UI + RPC (good density)

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Moon orbit menu: player picks an orbit slot; sends request to server for validation.
/// </summary>
void OnOrbitSlotClicked(int slotIndex)
{
    // --- Guard local state ---
    // [TITAN-ORBIT] Slot 0 is reserved for homeworld; UI hides it but we double-check.
    if (slotIndex < 1 || slotIndex > MaxSlots)
        return;

    // --- Ask server ---
    // [NETCODE] RPC — server decides if orbit is legal (range, team, cooldown).
    _rpcClient.SendMoonOrbitRequest(slotIndex);
}
```

### Data component (good density)

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Designer-tunable thrust cap for a ship class. Loaded from ShipPartCatalog ScriptableObject.
/// </summary>
public struct ShipMotorConfig : IComponentData
{
  /// <summary>Max speed in world units per second (top-down XZ plane).</summary>
    public float MaxSpeed;

    /// <summary>Acceleration in units/s². [TITAN-ORBIT] Used by ShipMotorSimulator, not Unity Rigidbody.</summary>
    public float Acceleration;
}
```

### Too thin (never ship like this)

```csharp
void LateUpdate()
{
    if (GhostPresentationTransformCache.TryGetLocalShip(out var pose))
        followTarget.SetPositionAndRotation(pose.Position, pose.Rotation);
}
```

